## 0. Your task

Build a single Tampermonkey userscript, `youtube-feed-summariser.user.js` (v2.2.1), that adds a **"Summarize"** item to the 3-dot menu of YouTube video cards and produces AI summaries (or transcripts) of videos **without opening them**, in Gmail-style dockable windows that live inside the YouTube tab. Then build a headless-browser test harness against a mock YouTube page and mock Gemini API, run it, and fix what fails. Deliver the script (and the test files) as files; do not paste the script into chat. Keep your final message short: what was built, what was tested, what is unverified.

Work incrementally: write the code in sections, `node --check` it, then run the tests. Do not ask clarifying questions; every decision you need is below. If a detail is not specified, choose the simplest robust option and note it.

Naming/continuity: keep `@name YouTube Feed Summariser (Gemini)` and `@namespace local.yt-feed-summariser` exactly, so pasting a new version over an old one **updates** it (and keeps its stored keys/cache) instead of installing a duplicate. UI strings use US spelling ("Summarize"); the `@name` keeps the British spelling.

