## 2. Platform constraints and quirks (critical)

- Userscript header: `@match https://www.youtube.com/*`, `@noframes`, `@run-at document-start`, grants `GM_xmlhttpRequest GM_getValue GM_setValue GM_deleteValue GM_listValues GM_addValueChangeListener GM_registerMenuCommand GM_addStyle GM_setClipboard`, `@connect generativelanguage.googleapis.com`, `@connect commons.wikimedia.org`. Wrap everything in one IIFE with `'use strict'`.
- **YouTube enforces Trusted Types**: never use `innerHTML`, `insertAdjacentHTML`, `DOMParser`, `outerHTML=` etc. Build all DOM with `createElement`/`textContent`/`append` (a tiny `h(tag, attrs, ...kids)` helper; attrs starting with `on` → addEventListener). SVG via `createElementNS`.
- All script UI lives in **one Shadow-DOM host** (`<div id="yt-ai-summary-host">` appended to `document.documentElement`, open shadow root) so YouTube CSS can't leak in. Use YouTube's CSS variables with fallbacks (`--yt-spec-base-background`, `--yt-spec-text-primary`, `--yt-spec-text-secondary`, `--yt-spec-10-percent-layer`, `--yt-spec-call-to-action`, `--yt-spec-badge-chip-background`) so it follows dark/light theme. The dock uses fixed dark-grey colours.
- Calls to Google use `GM_xmlhttpRequest` (bypasses CORS/CSP) with header `x-goog-api-key` (never put the key in the URL). Calls to YouTube itself (watch HTML, transcript endpoint) use same-origin `fetch`.
- **Keyboard**: because the UI is in a shadow root, YouTube hotkeys (k, f, m, /, …) would fire while typing. Register `keydown/keyup/keypress` listeners on `window` in the **capture phase at document-start**; for events whose `composedPath()` includes the host: `stopImmediatePropagation()` (never `preventDefault` except below). Ignore untrusted (`!e.isTrusted`) events. In that same handler: **Escape** → close the key dialog if open, else **minimize** the maximized window (never close); **Enter** (no Shift, not composing) inside a window's follow-up textarea → preventDefault + send.
- Page-level click handling is a single document-level **capture** listener; ignore clicks inside the host or on the injected menu item.
- Do not run a page-wide MutationObserver; poll briefly (see §5).

