## 4. Storage, caching, cross-tab sync

All persistence uses `GM_getValue/GM_setValue/GM_deleteValue/GM_listValues`. Tab identity: `TAB_ID = random`.

Keys: `keys` (array of `{id,name,key}`; migrate legacy single `gemini_api_key` into one key named "Default"), `opts`, `autoStart`, `lastModel`, `lastKeyId`, `lastSource`, `customModels`, `models_cache` (`{keyId:{ts,ids[]}}`), `cache_index` (`{storageKey: lastAccessTs}`), `sync_ping`, `win:<videoId>` (open-window registry), and cache entries:
`sum:<id>` summary-from-video · `trn:<id>` transcript-from-video · `sut:<id>` summary-from-transcript · `trt:<id>` transcript-from-captions. (Slot chosen by `mode` + `source`; helper `mk(win)` = mode + (source==='text' ? '+t' : ''); map `{summary:'sum:', transcript:'trn:', 'summary+t':'sut:', 'transcript+t':'trt:'}`.)

Cache entry: `{videoId,title,gen,text,sources,noSearch,notes,model,usedOpts,turns:[{q,a,sources,noSearch,notes,img}],images:{i1:{url,model,prompt}},fact:{text,sources,model,notes,ts}|null,ts,ts2}`. `ts2` changes on every write (used to detect remote updates). Eviction: when over `cacheMax`, delete least-recently-used entries **excluding videos with an open window**.

Window registry `win:<id>` = `{videoId,title,created,mode,source,status,busy,owner,hb,jobId,started,unread,errMsg,errCode,modelId,keyId,opts}`. `commit(win, quiet)` writes it and (unless quiet) writes `sync_ping={id,tab,t,n}`. Other tabs (via `GM_addValueChangeListener('sync_ping')`, ignoring their own `tab`) re-read just that window (`syncFromStorage(id)`): create it docked if new, apply changes if known, remove it if the meta is gone; `id==='*'` → full resync. A second listener on `keys` refreshes key dropdowns in other tabs. Also resync on `visibilitychange→visible`.

Job ownership: the tab running a job sets `owner=TAB_ID`, `jobId`, and writes `hb` every `heartbeatMs` (quiet commits). Other tabs show it as "…in another tab" and, if `hb` is older than `staleMs`, mark it failed ("interrupted") — checked in a 1 s timer. `pagehide` in the owner tab immediately writes status=error/INTERRUPTED. If another tab starts a new job on the same window (new `jobId`), the old owner cancels its job. On `DOMContentLoaded`, restore all `win:*` windows **minimized** (sorted by `created`), then run the model availability check (§8).

Rules: `maximized` is per-tab state, not shared; `unread` is shared (set on completion if the window is minimized **or** the tab is hidden; cleared on maximize). Closing a window deletes only its `win:` key — never the cache.

Opening (`openForVideo`): existing local window → maximize; registry entry from another tab → create + maximize; else create; if a cached result exists for the current mode+source (else try the other source) load it (status "done", labelled "cached <date>"), touch the cache, maximize — **no API call**; else if `autoStart` and (a key exists or model is Ask) start immediately and stay docked; else maximize the idle window (and open the key manager if no keys and model isn't Ask).

Tampermonkey menu commands: *Manage Gemini API keys*, *Re-check available Gemini models*, *Clear cached summaries (keeps open windows)*, *Close all summary windows*.

