## 8. Gemini API layer

`POST https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/<model>:generateContent`, header `x-goog-api-key`, body `{contents:[{role:'user',parts}], generationConfig?, tools?}`.

- `generationConfig`: `mediaResolution` (`MEDIA_RESOLUTION_LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH`; default LOW when `opts.mres` empty; **only for video calls**), `thinkingConfig:{thinkingLevel}` (low/medium/high), `responseMimeType:'application/json'` for the image-placement call.
- `tools`: `{google_search:{}}`, `{google_maps:{}}`, `{code_execution:{}}` per toggles (summary/follow-up calls; never in transcript mode).
- **Drop-and-retry** (up to 4 loops): 400 mentioning "resolution" → drop mediaResolution; 400 mentioning "think" → drop thinking level; tools enabled (unless `requireTools`) and (400 mentioning tool|search|ground|map|code|function, **or 429/403**) → drop all tools and remember reason (`unsupported`/`quota`). Dropped features are reported as a note ("ℹ <model> skipped: …"), and a ⚠ banner explains that grounding-dependent content then comes from the model's own knowledge.
- Response: join text parts excluding `thought`; empty → error ("returned no answer (<reason>) — video may be private, age-restricted, live, or too long"). Sources: dedupe `candidates[0].groundingMetadata.groundingChunks[].web.{uri,title}`.
- **Errors** (`apiError`): include `status`, `code:'QUOTA'` for 429, `retryMs` from `RetryInfo.retryDelay`, and for 429 the parsed `QuotaFailure` violations (`quotaId · model`) plus the **honest explanation**: it is a per-model/per-tool quota on the key; free-tier keys usually cannot use Pro models and cannot use Google Search grounding on Gemini 3.x; free tier also caps YouTube video input at 8 h/day (transcript source avoids it). Never present the 8-hour cap as *the* cause of a 429 that Flash-without-tools doesn't hit. Always append `API said: <raw message>`. 400+"api key" → "key rejected" (fatal). 403/404/5xx get specific hints.

**Model availability check** (at startup for every saved key, cached 5 min in `models_cache`, ⟳ forces): `GET /v1beta/models?pageSize=1000` (follow `nextPageToken`); a model is **usable** if its `supportedGenerationMethods` is empty or includes `generateContent` or anything matching /nteraction/i. Resolve a wanted id to itself or `<id>-preview`. If the check fails, show the recommended list marked "availability not verified".

