## 9. Retry and fallback policy

`runPolicy(win, job, makeSpec, {retries, fallback, startModel})`: per model, attempt `1+retries` times; fatal errors (NO_KEY, key rejected) throw immediately; retryable = anything except 404/403 or a `retryMs>60000`; wait `min(60 s, retryMs || 2.5 s×attempt)`; set `win.phase`. After a model is exhausted, record "⚠ <model> failed: <first line>" and, if `fallback` is on, move to **`nextModelDown`**: the next entry **below** the current one in `fallbackLadder` that the key can use (ids resolved against the live list; skip already-tried); a model not on the ladder starts at the first non-Pro entry. Attach the notes to the result (or to the thrown error). `retries` = `opts.retries` **only in Transcribe mode** (and for the caption fetch); everything else uses 0. Image placement and fact-check passes use the same policy with `fallback` per toggle.

