## 10. Fact-check, sources, images

**Fact-check/sources pass** (separate call after the summary, so it can use a different model that has Search access on free keys): model = `opts.factModel` or auto (first of `factPreferred` available on the key, else the summary model; for Ask → default model). Prompt: "You are checking a summary of a YouTube video titled … Use Google Search. Sections: `## Fact-check` (claims with [MM:SS], verdicts ✅ Supported / ⚠️ Partly true / ❌ Contradicted / ❓ Unverifiable, 1–2 sentences evidence; skip opinions) if `fc`; `## Further reading` (3–8 authoritative links as Markdown links) if `src`. Only URLs from search results. Do not repeat the summary." + the summary (≤30 000 chars). Call with `{google_search:{}}` and **`requireTools:true`** (no silent dropping — if it fails, show the error in the box with Retry). Result rendered in the **fact box below the summary** with its own model dropdown + Run/Re-run, plus deduped "Sources consulted (Google Search)" list; stored in the cache entry. Auto-runs after a successful summary when `fc||src`; the box also shows when the user turned either on but hasn't run it.

**Frames** (`[[FRAME mm:ss | caption]]`): fetch `/watch?v=<id>` HTML, regex `"playerStoryboardSpecRenderer":{"spec":"…"}`, `JSON.parse` the string, split on `|`: first part is the base URL with `$L`/`$N`; each level `w#h#count#cols#rows#intervalMs#name#sigh` (ignore intervalMs=0); use the highest level; sheet = floor(idx/(cols·rows)); URL = base with `$L`=level index, `$N`=name with `$M`→sheet, plus `&sigh=<encoded>`; show as a CSS background sprite (scaled to ~400 px) with a "▶ mm:ss" badge; click → in-window player at that second. Best-effort low-res preview; cached per video in memory.

**Commons images** (`[[IMG terms | caption]]`): `GM_xmlhttpRequest` to `commons.wikimedia.org/w/api.php?action=query&format=json&generator=search&gsrnamespace=6&gsrlimit=6&gsrsearch=<terms> filetype:bitmap|drawing&prop=imageinfo&iiprop=url|extmetadata|size&iiurlwidth=720`; first result with width ≥300; show thumb linked to the file page with licence + artist (strip tags) in the caption; remove the figure on failure.

**AI images** (`opts.gen`, summary mode, non-Ask): Gemini **designs** `[[GEN prompt | caption]]` markers in the summary (max 3) → the script strips them and **calls the image model for each prompt** with the user's parameters → the finished images (shrunk) are **sent back to Gemini** (text + `inline_data` image parts, `responseMimeType:'application/json'`) which replies `{"placements":[{"image":k,"after":"<25–80 chars copied verbatim>","caption":"…"}]}` → the script inserts `[[IMAGE k | caption]]` after the end of the block containing that excerpt (normalized-substring match; sort inserts descending by line then descending k so lower k ends up first; unmatched/failed placement → append at end with a ⚠ note). Renderer shows `[[IMAGE k]]` from `win.images['i'+k]` labelled "AI-generated illustration (<model name>) · may contain inaccuracies". Images are stored (JPEG ≤960 px, quality .85, via canvas) in the cache entry and **never auto-regenerated** on reopen.
- **Image chain**: if `opts.imgModel` set → that model (+ lower-ranked ones only if `fallback`); else tier by the *text* model: id contains "pro" → start at index 0; contains "lite" → index 3; else index 1; filter to models the key can use. Try each; 400/404 → drop optional features one at a time in this order (image search tool, thinking, imageSize, aspectRatio) and retry; "does not support generateContent"/404 → retry via the **Interactions API**; any other error (429/5xx) → next model.
- `generateContent` body: `generationConfig:{responseModalities: imgOut==='image' ? ['IMAGE'] : ['TEXT','IMAGE'], imageConfig:{aspectRatio,imageSize}?, thinkingConfig:{thinkingLevel}?}`, `tools:[{google_search:{searchTypes:{webSearch:{},imageSearch:{}}}}]` if image search. Parse `inlineData`/`inline_data`.
- `POST /v1beta/interactions` body: `{model, input:[{type:'text',text}], response_format:{type:'image',mime_type:'image/jpeg',aspect_ratio?,image_size?}, generation_config:{thinking_level}?, tools:[{type:'google_search',search_types:['web_search','image_search']}]?}`; find the first object with `type==='image'` and `data` in the response. **[UNVERIFIED against the live API]**
- Prefix every image prompt with "Create a clean, clear, accurate illustration."

