## 11. YouTube transcript source

Route A (preferred): same-origin `fetch('/watch?v=<id>')`; regex `"getTranscriptEndpoint":{"params":"([^"]+)"`, `"INNERTUBE_API_KEY":"…"`, `"INNERTUBE_CONTEXT_CLIENT_VERSION":"…"`; `POST /youtubei/v1/get_transcript?prettyPrint=false&key=<key>` with `{context:{client:{clientName:'WEB',clientVersion,hl:'en'}},params}`; walk the JSON for `transcriptSegmentRenderer` → `{startMs, snippet.runs[].text | snippet.simpleText}`.
Route B (fallback): hidden watch page (§12 helper) → click `ytd-video-description-transcript-section-renderer button[aria-label]` (or `chip-view-model button[aria-label="Transcript"]`) → wait up to 20 s for `ytd-engagement-panel-section-list-renderer[target-id="engagement-panel-searchable-transcript"|"PAmodern_transcript_view"][visibility="ENGAGEMENT_PANEL_VISIBILITY_EXPANDED"]` whose `innerText` parses to ≥2 segments; parse generically: a line matching `^(?:\d{1,2}:)?\d{1,2}:\d{2}$` starts a segment (also `ts text` on one line), following lines are its text.
Format as `[MM:SS] text` lines (padded minutes; `H:MM:SS` over an hour), cap `maxTranscriptChars`, cache per video in memory. Both routes fail → error code `TRANSCRIPT` ("Couldn't get this video's transcript (…)"). **[UNVERIFIED on live YouTube]**

