## 12. YouTube "Ask" provider (no API, no key)

An entry **"YouTube Ask (Gemini in the page)"** at the top of the model dropdown. Summaries/follow-ups only; Source forced to Video; Images/AI-images disabled (Fact-check/Sources still run afterwards through Gemini if a key exists). It drives a **hidden same-origin copy of the watch page**:

- `hiddenWatchFrame`: `<iframe src="/watch?v=<id>" title="YouTube Ask helper (hidden)" allow="autoplay 'none'">` positioned `fixed; left:-20000px; width:1400px; height:900px; opacity:0; pointer-events:none`, appended to `documentElement`; `job.abort` removes it; always removed in `finally`; videos inside are paused/muted when playing; remember `document.activeElement` and restore focus at the end. A semaphore limits concurrent hidden pages to `askConcurrency` (extra jobs show "Queued").
- Steps (poll with `waitFor`, honour `job.cancelled`): (1) find an **Ask entry button** `.you-chat-entrypoint-button button` — **choose a visible one, preferring the one inside `ytd-watch-metadata`; never the player's fullscreen-only one (inside `.html5-video-player`, hidden, first in DOM order)**; none within `askLoadMs` → error "YouTube's Ask button didn't appear… needs you to be signed in… pick a Gemini model" (code `ASK`). (2) click it; wait for `ytd-engagement-panel-section-list-renderer[target-id="PAyouchat"][visibility="ENGAGEMENT_PANEL_VISIBILITY_EXPANDED"]` and `textarea.chatInputViewModelChatInput` (retry once with a full pointer-event sequence). (3) wait until the number of `you-chat-item-view-model` elements is stable ~1.2 s (greetings/chips), record the baseline. (4) **send ladder**, checking after each that an item containing the first 40 chars of the prompt appeared (and `items().length > baseline`): re-query the textarea each time (it can re-render); *typing* = `window.focus(); ta.focus(); ta.select(); document.execCommand('insertText', false, prompt)` (fallback native value setter); then wait ≤2.5 s for `.chatInputViewModelChatInputForm button[aria-label="Send"]` to be enabled (not `disabled`, `aria-disabled!=='true'`) and click it; *input events* = native setter + `InputEvent('input',{inputType:'insertText'})` + `change` + `keyup`; *Enter* keydown on the textarea; *form submit* = **dispatch a `submit` event (never `requestSubmit()`, which can navigate the hidden page away)**; *forced click* = remove `disabled`/`aria-disabled` from Send and click; finally, for summaries only, click the first chip `button.ytwYouChatChipsDataChip` whose text matches `/summari[sz]e/i` (adds note that sponsor filtering isn't applied). All fail → throw "Ask's Send button never became available (tried: …). Details were written to the browser console." and `console.warn` `{tried, textareaChars, send:{disabled,ariaDisabled}, formFound}` + the first 2500 chars of `yt-chat-input-view-model.outerHTML`. (5) answer = the last `markdown-div` inside items **after** the item that holds our question (fallback after 8 s: items after the baseline); finished when its text is unchanged for `askStableMs` and `yt-item-section-renderer[data-target-id="youchat_messages_section"]` isn't `aria-busy="true"`; timeout `askAnswerMs`.
- **DOM→Markdown** (`domToMarkdown`): skip `button/svg/img/style/script/noscript/yt-icon/yt-touch-feedback-shape` and hidden/aria-hidden; h1/h2→`##`, h3+→`###`, p blocks, ul/ol with 2-space nesting (`- `/`1. `), strong/em/code/pre, `br`, table rows as `- a | b`; anchors whose text is a timestamp become `[mm:ss]` (so the renderer makes them in-window player links); other `http(s)` links kept, YouTube `/redirect?q=` unwrapped; collapse blank lines. Everything downstream (cache, follow-ups, rendering) therefore reuses the Markdown path.
- **Ask prompts**: summary — "Write a detailed, well-organised summary of this video in English. Use headings, short paragraphs and bullet points, and start each section with a [MM:SS] timestamp. Cover the specific claims, arguments, examples, numbers and conclusions, in order, then finish with 3-5 key takeaways. Leave out sponsor segments and ad reads, and any self-promotion by the creator (merchandise, Patreon/memberships, donations, unrelated charities, tour dates, their other products, courses or channels, "like and subscribe"): do not mention them at all." Follow-up — a fresh hidden page each time with: "Earlier you wrote this summary of this video: """<≤5000 chars>""" [last 3 Q/A, clipped] Now answer this follow-up question about the video, accurately and concisely: <q>".
- Verified (from user-supplied page markup): panel `target-id="PAyouchat"`, entry buttons (under-video "Ask", description "Ask questions", fullscreen quick action), greeting items, chips ("Summarise the video", …), `form.chatInputViewModelChatInputForm` with `textarea.chatInputViewModelChatInput` and a Send button that is `disabled="true"` until text is entered. The Ask button only exists when signed in. **[Root cause of "Send never became available" on live YouTube is UNCONFIRMED; the ladder + diagnostics exist for that reason.]**

