## 13. Markdown renderer (DOM-building, no HTML parsing)

Supports headings (`#`/`##`→h3, deeper→h4), paragraphs, `-`/`*`/`•`/`1.` lists with one nested level (indent ≥2), `---`, **bold**, *italic*, `code`, `[text](http(s)://…)` (new tab, noopener), and `[mm:ss]` / `[h:mm:ss]` timestamps → anchors (`class=ts`, real `watch?v=&t=` href, plain click `preventDefault` + seek the in-window player; modified clicks open normally). Marker lines `[[FRAME …]]`, `[[IMG …]]`, `[[GEN …]]`, `[[IMAGE k | …]]` must be on their own line (pre-normalise inline occurrences onto separate lines); honoured only when the corresponding option was used for that result, capped (`maxVisuals`, `maxGenImages`); otherwise dropped. Raw `<script>` text must show as literal text.

